{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9MzspV6XqnBVaR6Ah3bDg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→=== Harness initialized: 2026-03-19T21:39:25+09:00 ===\n     2→Project type: java-maven\n     3→\n     4→=== Session 2026-03-19T21:54:16+09:00 ===\n     5→Completed: Item 1 - Employee model class\n     6→Changes: Created Employee.java in com.example.legacy.model with all 8 fields (id, name, email, department, salary, hireDate, createdAt, updatedAt). Added @JsonFormat annotations for date serialization: hireDate as \"yyyy-MM-dd\", createdAt/updatedAt as \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss\". Also fixed pom.xml jackson.version from 2.9.11.1 (nonexistent) to 2.9.10.8. Created EmployeeSerializationTest.java with 5 unit tests covering Jackson date serialization.\n     7→Why: @JsonFormat defaults to UTC, but spec requires server timezone; ObjectMapper must call setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) to propagate local TZ to @JsonFormat patterns.\n     8→Discovered: jackson-databind 2.9.11.1 does not exist in Maven Central — corrected to 2.9.10.8. All subsequent items should use this version.\n     9→Difficulty: S as planned, but timezone subtlety added ~10 min debugging.\n    10→\n    11→=== Session 2026-03-19T22:10:00+09:00 ===\n    12→Completed: Item 2 - Request/Response DTOs\n    13→Changes: Created EmployeeRequest.java and ErrorResponse.java in com.example.legacy.dto. EmployeeRequest has 5 fields with validation annotations. ErrorResponse has status/message/timestamp fields plus nested FieldError inner class for validation error details.\n    14→Why: javax.validation 1.1.0.Final lacks @NotBlank and @Email; used org.hibernate.validator.constraints for those two. Standard javax.validation.constraints used for @NotNull, @Size, @DecimalMin.\n    15→Discovered: javax.validation 1.1 annotation gap — @NotBlank and @Email require Hibernate Validator's own constraints package in this stack.\n    16→Difficulty: S as planned; 5 min to diagnose annotation package issue.\n    17→\n    18→=== Session 2026-03-19T22:00:00+09:00 ===\n    19→Completed: Item 3 - Database schema and test resources\n    20→Changes: Created src/main/resources/schema.sql (PostgreSQL DDL with BIGSERIAL), src/test/resources/schema.sql (H2-compatible DDL with BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT), src/test/resources/application-test.properties (H2 in-memory MODE=PostgreSQL config).\n    21→Why: Used separate DDL files per profile instead of relying on H2 PostgreSQL mode to support BIGSERIAL — avoids runtime DDL failures and is more explicit. H2 test schema uses DROP TABLE IF EXISTS + CREATE TABLE (no IF NOT EXISTS) to ensure clean state per test run.\n    22→Discovered: No new discoveries. Followed plan: BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT for H2, BIGSERIAL for PostgreSQL, MODE=PostgreSQL in JDBC URL for H2 compatibility.\n    23→Difficulty: S as planned.\n    24→\n    25→=== Session 2026-03-19T22:03:00+09:00 ===\n    26→Completed: Item 4 - Spring application and database configuration\n    27→Changes: Created AppConfig.java (@Configuration, @ComponentScan, @PropertySource), DatabaseConfig.java (DBCP2 DataSource, SqlSessionFactoryBean with type aliases + mapper locations, DataSourceTransactionManager, static MapperScannerConfigurer), WebConfig.java (@EnableWebMvc, Jackson ObjectMapper with local TZ, CORS), WebInitializer.java (AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer), application.properties (PostgreSQL defaults).\n    28→Why: MapperScannerConfigurer is a BeanDefinitionRegistryPostProcessor that runs before @Value properties are resolved — declared static @Bean to avoid premature injection failures. ObjectMapper configured with setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) per LEARNINGS.md for correct @JsonFormat behavior.\n    29→Discovered: No new discoveries. Static @Bean pattern for MapperScannerConfigurer is the standard mitigation for BDRPP ordering issue.\n    30→Difficulty: M as planned.\n    31→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e01a63f-0965-4a14-ba7a-31cb19b2c8f2","uuid":"fde02198-2a40-45aa-b42e-51cbadc4e4ec","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/progress.txt","content":"=== Harness initialized: 2026-03-19T21:39:25+09:00 ===\nProject type: java-maven\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T21:54:16+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 1 - Employee model class\nChanges: Created Employee.java in com.example.legacy.model with all 8 fields (id, name, email, department, salary, hireDate, createdAt, updatedAt). Added @JsonFormat annotations for date serialization: hireDate as \"yyyy-MM-dd\", createdAt/updatedAt as \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss\". Also fixed pom.xml jackson.version from 2.9.11.1 (nonexistent) to 2.9.10.8. Created EmployeeSerializationTest.java with 5 unit tests covering Jackson date serialization.\nWhy: @JsonFormat defaults to UTC, but spec requires server timezone; ObjectMapper must call setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) to propagate local TZ to @JsonFormat patterns.\nDiscovered: jackson-databind 2.9.11.1 does not exist in Maven Central — corrected to 2.9.10.8. All subsequent items should use this version.\nDifficulty: S as planned, but timezone subtlety added ~10 min debugging.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:10:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 2 - Request/Response DTOs\nChanges: Created EmployeeRequest.java and ErrorResponse.java in com.example.legacy.dto. EmployeeRequest has 5 fields with validation annotations. ErrorResponse has status/message/timestamp fields plus nested FieldError inner class for validation error details.\nWhy: javax.validation 1.1.0.Final lacks @NotBlank and @Email; used org.hibernate.validator.constraints for those two. Standard javax.validation.constraints used for @NotNull, @Size, @DecimalMin.\nDiscovered: javax.validation 1.1 annotation gap — @NotBlank and @Email require Hibernate Validator's own constraints package in this stack.\nDifficulty: S as planned; 5 min to diagnose annotation package issue.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:00:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 3 - Database schema and test resources\nChanges: Created src/main/resources/schema.sql (PostgreSQL DDL with BIGSERIAL), src/test/resources/schema.sql (H2-compatible DDL with BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT), src/test/resources/application-test.properties (H2 in-memory MODE=PostgreSQL config).\nWhy: Used separate DDL files per profile instead of relying on H2 PostgreSQL mode to support BIGSERIAL — avoids runtime DDL failures and is more explicit. H2 test schema uses DROP TABLE IF EXISTS + CREATE TABLE (no IF NOT EXISTS) to ensure clean state per test run.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Followed plan: BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT for H2, BIGSERIAL for PostgreSQL, MODE=PostgreSQL in JDBC URL for H2 compatibility.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:03:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 4 - Spring application and database configuration\nChanges: Created AppConfig.java (@Configuration, @ComponentScan, @PropertySource), DatabaseConfig.java (DBCP2 DataSource, SqlSessionFactoryBean with type aliases + mapper locations, DataSourceTransactionManager, static MapperScannerConfigurer), WebConfig.java (@EnableWebMvc, Jackson ObjectMapper with local TZ, CORS), WebInitializer.java (AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer), application.properties (PostgreSQL defaults).\nWhy: MapperScannerConfigurer is a BeanDefinitionRegistryPostProcessor that runs before @Value properties are resolved — declared static @Bean to avoid premature injection failures. ObjectMapper configured with setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) per LEARNINGS.md for correct @JsonFormat behavior.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Static @Bean pattern for MapperScannerConfigurer is the standard mitigation for BDRPP ordering issue.\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}}}
